\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia higher despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worries  \b0\par\par\uc2 854 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2006\par 03:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 30 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against the dollar on Thursday, buoyed by economic fundamentals justifying their underlying strength, despite lingering market concerns about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But a spike in crude oil prices capped gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while traders continued to be wary of regional central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Thio Chin Loo, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas, said she remained bullish about the near-term strength of most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of funds flowing into Asian equity markets.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks likely a quite good picture for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The only ones seeing less inflows are the Philippines and Indonesia because they have been front-runners, so there is a bit of consolidation as markets move from the high-yielder to the laggard," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a fresh nine-year high of 1.5421 against the U.S. dollar before retreating to 1.5440, while the South Korean won <KRW=> reversed earlier losses to hit around 929 per dollar, slightly off a nine-year high this week of 925.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> hit 32.42 per U.S. dollar, the highest level in 4-\u189\'00\'BD months as exporters tried to offload their dollar holdings.  \par \par \uc2 "Sentiment is quite firm and when you see price action on the Korean won, where everyday you get comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, it is testiment to strength in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank.  \par \par \uc2 RUNNING AHEAD  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> gained about a third of a percent versus the dollar to 36 per dollar, hitting its strongest level in almost eight years.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Thailand will not resist a lower dollar/baht if the broad global trend is for a lower dollar," said Philip Wee, DBS Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.  \par \par \uc2 But based on current euro/dollar and dollar/yen levels, the baht should be closer to 36.40 per dollar, he said. The euro <EUR=> was trading around $1.3145, having come off Wednesday's 20-month highs, while the yen weakened to 116.50 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "This sort of tells you why Bank of Thailand is uncomfortable that the baht strength may have run ahead of itself," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand (BOT) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  both verbally and by buying dollars this week, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The BOT said on Wednesday the baht had risen too fast and its rise was not justified by fundamentals. On Monday it had said it would ask the finance ministry to allow exporters to hold their overseas receipts for up to 15 days instead of the seven-day limit now in place.  \par \par \uc2 Shahab Jalinoos of ABN AMRO Bank said baht had risen this year on higher baht interest rates and the relative cheapness of Thai stocks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained about 14 percent so far this year despite months of political uncertainty that culminated in a bloodless coup in September.  \par \par \uc2 The strength of the trade account, which has propelled Thailand's current account to swing into surplus in the later half of this year, was also behind the baht's rally, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "Until now, strong global demand has overwhelmed the effect of baht strength, allowing exports growth to remain solid.  \par \par \uc2 "If the data show more evidence that this is still the case, we see room for further baht gains through 36.00 towards 35.50, given that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already thrown in the towel on its ability to stop this trend," Jalinoos said in a note to clients. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0819 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.13         116.01       -0.10\par  Sing dlr        1.5431         1.5454       +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr      32.415         32.495       +0.25\par  Korean won      929.10         930.50       +0.15\par  Baht             36.00          36.12       +0.33\par  Peso             49.64          49.71       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9167.00        9162.00       -0.05\par  Rupee            44.75          44.69       -0.13\par  Ringgit         3.6180         3.6280       +0.28\par  Yuan            7.8333         7.8340       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.13         117.96       +1.58\par  Sing dlr        1.5431         1.6625       +7.74\par  Taiwan dlr      32.415         32.850       +1.34\par  Korean won      929.10        1011.60       +8.88\par  Baht             36.00          41.11      +14.19\par  Peso             49.64          53.09       +6.95\par  Rupiah         9167.00        9835.00       +7.29\par  Rupee            44.75          45.04       +0.65\par  Ringgit         3.6180         3.7790       +4.45