\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  worries cap Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2006\par 03:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Monday as the dollar took a beating against the euro and yen, but wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength dampened the bullish sentiment slightly.  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> was quoted at its highest level in more than nine years at 925 per dollar, before paring gains on suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said the baht's rise had been too fast and it might allow exporters to hold dollars for up to 15 days, longer than the current 7-day limit. The baht <THB=> was capped at about 36.38 per dollar, a hair's breadth away from 7-1/2-year highs of 36.36 struck earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> gained almost 0.7 percent to 32.62 to the U.S. dollar, its highest since mid-August, before paring some gains. The Philippine peso <PHP=> ended local trade off a fresh 4-1/2-year high at 49.60 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2  "Dollar weakness pressure was felt first in Asia," said Mirza Baig, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the regional central banks had reined the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in, he said.  \par \par \uc2  "Now, the G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have taken up the torch, and emerging Asia is lagging."  \par \par \uc2  The euro hit a 20-month peak at about $1.3180 <EUR=> on electronic trading platform EBS and the dollar fell to a three-month low at 115.40 yen <JPY=> on Monday.  \par \par \uc2  Although the dollar subsequently clawed back some ground against the majors, analysts suggested the Asian rally would continue even if they had underperformed so far.  \par \par \uc2  "The fundamental picture continues to shift in favour of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaining in strength and it would be reasonable to expect local central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Richard Yetsenga, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2  "But Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have underperformed the move in the majors versus the dollar."  \par \par \uc2  Expectations for further euro zone interest rate increases have bolstered the euro. The dollar, in general, has also been hurt by position adjusting and ongoing talk of central banks diversifying their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves away from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Some traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be limited in the face of a strong dollar downtrend.  \par \par \uc2  "They (the central banks) will come in on and off, but I don't think they will be too aggressive because dollar sentiment is very bearish," said a Singapore dollar trader.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=>, meanwhile, retreated to 1.5515/25 per U.S. dollar, up about 0.15 percent from levels traded late on Friday but off a nine-year high hit last week at 1.5467.  \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> firmed to 7.8410 to the dollar, its strongest level since the July 2005 revaluation and analysts continued to expect a further pick-up in gains.  \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yuan is now under major pressure to move lower quickly given the influence of euro/dollar and dollar/yen," ABN AMRO \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Shahab Jalinoos said in a note.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0840 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.11         115.99       -0.10\par  Sing dlr        1.5519         1.5540       +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      32.700         32.833       +0.41\par  Korean won      930.50         931.90       +0.15\par  Baht             36.39          36.53       +0.38\par  Peso             49.66          49.71       +0.10\par  Rupiah         9136.00        9155.00       +0.21\par  Rupee            44.65          44.79       +0.31\par  Ringgit         3.6350         3.6370       +0.06\par  Yuan            7.8440         7.8547       +0.14\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.11         117.96       +1.59\par  Sing dlr        1.5519         1.6625       +7.13\par  Taiwan dlr      32.700         32.850       +0.46\par  Korean won      930.50        1011.60       +8.72\par  Baht             36.39          41.11      +12.97\par  Peso             49.66          53.09       +6.91\par  Rupiah         9136.00        9835.00       +7.65\par  Rupee            44.65          45.04       +0.87\par  Ringgit         3.6350         3.7790       +3.96\par  Yuan            7.8440         8.0702       +2.88\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061130e2br0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip