\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down On Rumored MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2006\par 07:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5576   +0.0042 \par  Overnight Rate        3.13%    +7bps \par  2 Year Bond Yield     3.02%    -3bps \par  10-Year Bond Yield    3.02%    -2bps \par  2-Year Swap Offer     3.44%    +2bps \par  10-Year Swap Offer    3.40%    +1bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve  -4 bps   -1bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell considerably against the U.S. dollar in afternoon trades in Asia Friday on rumored \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "The market is quite cautious of the downside of USD/SGD next week with the presence of the official bid," a local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist said. "The buying is more frequent than historically."  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar, which was trading below S$1.5500 before the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulled up to S$1.5582 around 0452 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS' key monetary policy tool is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band. It doesn't traditionally comment on any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "If the pace of decline of the U.S. dollar is fast again next week to uncomfortable levels, the MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," BNP Paribas \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thio Chin Loo said.  \par \par \uc2 She predicts that the greenback will continue to be soft next week.  \par \par \uc2 "With more U.S. data such as October home salesand a lot of speeches by Fed officials upcoming, the market is going to price in interest rate cuts by the Fed," she said. This is because the data are supposed to signal a weak housing market.  \par \par \uc2 The first strategist didn't rule out the possibility of the U.S. dollar revisiting this week's low of S$1.5481 if it continues to be bearish against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Thio said there isn't much support for the U.S. unit until S$1.5400, and the next level of support would be at S$1.5250.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore bond curve was flat.  \par \par \uc2 "A local bank has been selling its two-year bonds since yesterday, while the long end is still in demand," a local bank dealer said. "The yield curve will likely remain flat next week as there are still consistent offers and bids at the respective ends of the curve."  \par \par \uc2 The two-year bond rose on persistent demand despite selling by the local bank.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. October home sales data next week will influence local bonds since participants have no other news to track, another local bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 24-11-06 0644GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061124e2bo0007s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
