\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dlr near 9-yr high, market wary of cbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2006\par 02:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 23 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar on Thursday hovered near a nine-year high set against the U.S. dollar in offshore trade, but markets were wary about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=> traded at 1.5525 to the U.S. dollar -- within sight of a high of about 1.5520 touched overnight as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under broad-based selling pressure.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the Singapore dollar was probably trading on the strong side of its secret trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  Singapore (MAS) could step into the market to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening too quickly.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no sign so far of the MAS, but definitely the market will be cautious at this level," said a trader in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say there have been signs that the MAS has already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market this week.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061123e2bn0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
