  \par \par \uc2 "If there's another interest rate hike in Japan, it would also encourage more traders to stay short dollar against the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  till the end of the year," the strategist said.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore bonds market, there was aggressive selling in the two-year bonds to take advantage of higher yields offered by the three-month treasury bills.  \par \par \uc2 But, bond trading is "likely to remain range-bound for the rest of the month," said one local bank dealer. "The U.S. data are very mixed; there's strong employment, weak housing data, and so on. The market is still trying to get the whole picture."  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4036; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 21-11-06 0741GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061121e2bl000sc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
