\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -S.Korean won recovers, other Asians steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2006\par 03:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The South Korean won recovered some ground it had lost to the dollar over the past couple of days, helped by a large bout of dollar inflows on Thursday for local businesses and by the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also stabilised as markets waited for U.S. consumer prices data to give them a sense of direction for Federal Reserve policy.  \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen <JPY=> rallied briefly to 117.75 per dollar on a report that China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been buying yen for its reserves but soon gave up those gains, pushing the dollar to levels near 118 yen traded overnight after the Fed said in minutes of its October meeting that reducing inflation was its biggest concern.  \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many of which had hit multi-month and multi-year highs at the start of this week, slipped in early deals but stabilised subsequently.  \par \par \uc2  After hitting a six-month high of 927.8 per dollar on Monday, the won <KRW=> had gradually lost ground this week, falling earlier on Thursday to around 944 per dollar, its weakest level since late October.  \par \par \uc2  However, by 0730 GMT, it had rebounded slightly to be quoted around 937 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2  "The upside in dollar/won changed to downside as the yen rose and offshore markets sold dollars," said Yun Jin Ko, a dealer with Kookmin Bank in Seoul.  \par \par \uc2  "Exporters of ships and electronics joined in," she said.  \par \par \uc2  Mirza Baig, Deutsche Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist said a surge in export orders for Korean manufacturers of ships, oil platforms and power plants had created a steady stream of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings, putting pressure on the won to appreciate.  \par \par \uc2  "The absence of the Bank of Korea makes it easier for spot to fall," he said.  \par \par \uc2  Fearing rapid and volatile appreciation in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , central banks in South Korea, Thailand and India are suspected of having sold their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. Traders estimated Bank of Korea had bought about $1.5 billion on Monday and Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2  Baig said only a few exporters seemed to be testing the Bank of Korea's tolerance.  \par \par \uc2   "Not all segments of the market play this cat and mouse game with BOK. Exporters generally just want a good level to sell," he said.  \par \par \uc2  WON, RUPEE CAPPED?  \par \par \uc2  Gerrard Katz, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading for North Asia at Standard Chartered Bank, said this stream of export earnings will put a floor under the won, despite the Bank of Korea's attempts to rein it in.  \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/won will find 945-950 tough resistance. I heard a lot of exporters forecast a 900-940 range for next year so they will be (dollar) sellers," he said.  \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Singapore dollar <SGD=> fell to 1.5611 per U.S. dollar in early trades, having gradually come off the 9-year highs around 1.5545 hit this week. It then pared back to be traded at 1.5575/80.  \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee <INR=IN> rallied nearly half a percent from Wednesday's close near 45.34 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2  JPMorgan Chase said in a note to clients the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) remained high with the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted level now estimated to be at the top end of the MAS's secret policy band.  \par \par \uc2  It also said the Reserve Bank of India's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had moved the rupee's inflation-adjusted trade-weighted levels away from overvalued territory, and that it was technically now more favourable to be buying the rupee <INR=IN>.  \par \par \uc2  "Foreigners remain net buyers of local equities and oil prices below $60 a barrel should sustain market impetus for dollar/rupee downside," JPMorgan said.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   Change on the day at 0733 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.04         117.75       -0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.5580         1.5589       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      32.835         32.808       -0.08\par  Korean won      937.40         941.30       +0.42\par  Baht             36.46          36.52       +0.16\par  Peso             50.08          50.07       -0.02\par  Rupiah         9163.00        9175.00       +0.13\par  Rupee            45.15          45.34       +0.43\par  Ringgit         3.6520         3.6460       -0.16\par  Yuan            7.8688         7.8676       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.04         117.96       -0.07\par  Sing dlr        1.5580         1.6625       +6.71\par  Taiwan dlr      32.835         32.850       +0.05\par  Korean won      937.40        1011.60       +7.92\par  Baht             36.46          41.11      +12.75\par  Peso             50.08          53.09       +6.01\par  Rupiah         9163.00        9835.00       +7.33\par  Rupee            45.15          45.04       -0.23\par  Ringgit      