\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Higher on China reserves plan, yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2006\par 04:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against the dollar on Friday supported by news of China's plans to diversify its $1 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and a firmer Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar lost ground against the yen <JPY=> and the euro <EUR=> after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had a clear plan to diversify its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, although it was not clear whether China would sell dollar assets.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> rose as high as 932.40 against the dollar on Friday, brushing a six-month high after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief expressed concern about a sharp unwinding of carry trades in the low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are taking their cue from the yen and the yuan," said Philip Wee, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a quite a bit of interest in the yen and this is supportive."  \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Zhou Xiaochuan told Reuters on Thursday that China had a clear plan to diversify its reserves. On Friday, he said such diversification would be across different \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and investment instruments in emerging markets.  \par \par \uc2 Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists expect Beijing to face greater foreign pressure to let the yuan rise faster after the country posted a record trade surplus of $23.83 billion for October.  \par \par \uc2 China's yuan <CNY=CFXS> rose as far as to 7.8633 per dollar on Friday, its strongest level since the July 2005 revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 RALLY VS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 A further rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards the end of the year is widely expected, but some analysts also fear that recent strength in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  might trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid concerns about a possible export slowdown.  \par \par \uc2 "Lower global rates encourage risk-taking among developed country investors, implying increased flow into emerging markets asset classes", Richard Yetsenga at HSBC said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 Yun Jin Ko, a dealer at Kookmim Bank, said she saw no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of Korea on Friday, but cautioned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step in if the won rises above the 930 mark.  \par \par \uc2 "I still believe 930 is our supporting line with probable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=> gained nearly a quarter of a percent and traded as high as 1.5565 per U.S. dollar, close to nine-year highs around 1.5560 reached earlier in November.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> firmed to T$32.78, just off a seven-week high reached on Wednesday, while the Thai baht <THB=> traded in a narrow range between 36.59 and 36.67 per dollar, near Wednesday's seven-year high of 36.56.  \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee <INR=IN> rose to about 44.35 per dollar on Friday, its strongest level in nearly eight months, before retreating to around 44.60.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers in India said state-banks were selling rupees for dollars in suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0815 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.52         117.74       +0.19\par  Sing dlr        1.5578         1.5617       +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr      32.810         32.870       +0.18\par  Korean won      933.90         936.40       +0.27\par  Baht             36.63          36.67       +0.11\par  Peso             49.89          49.95       +0.12\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9119.00       +0.04\par  Rupee            44.62          44.55       -0.16\par  Ringgit         3.6400         3.6440       +0.11\par  Yuan            7.8652         7.8665       +0.02\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.52         117.96       +0.37\par  Sing dlr        1.5578         1.6625       +6.72\par  Taiwan dlr      32.810         32.850       +0.12\par  Korean won      933.90        1011.60       +8.32\par  Baht             36.63          41.11      +12.23\par  Peso             49.89          53.09       +6.41\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9835.00       +7.90\par  Rupee            44.62          45.04       +0.94\par  Ringgit         3.6400         3.7790       +3.82\par  Yuan            7.8652         8.0702       +2.61\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061113e2ba0006y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
