\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Gains On Weak U.S. Data; Bonds Rally  \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2006\par 08:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5575   -0.0043 \par  Overnight Rate        3.63%    +1 bp \par  2 Year Bond Yield     2.99%    -4 bps \par  10-Year Bond Yield    3.12%    -5 bps \par  2-Year Swap Offer     3.47%    -5 bps \par  10-Year Swap Offer    3.57%    -6 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve  10 bps   -1 bp \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar gained in Asian trade Wednesday following issue of weak U.S. data overnight.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Despite possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said the U.S. unit is likely to remain bearish for the rest of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS' key monetary policy tool is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 "It is going to be dependent on the U.S. dollar outlook, considering there's hardly any local stimulus in the near term," said a foreign bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "After weak Chicago PMI (Purchasing Managing Index) yesterday, the dollar fell again. What we can do now is to keep looking out for U.S. data, like the October U.S. non-farm payrolls this Friday," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The National Association of Purchasing Management Chicago said Tuesday its index of area business activity fell to 53.5 in October on a seasonally adjusted basis from 62.1 in September.  \par \par \uc2 Overseas Chinese Banking Corp. said in a report that the U.S. dollar is likely to stay pressured against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the International Monetary Bank's renewed call for Chinese yuan flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 "It's going to be a strong Singapore dollar story in the long term," said a second foreign bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 Kelvin Ng, a technical strategist from Ideaglobal, expects the U.S. unit to fall to a low of S$1.5525 within the next four weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds rallied, tracking U.S. Treasurys after the weak Chicago data.  \par \par \uc2 "The bonds are likely to be quite supported before the non-farm payroll data this Friday," said one local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "If Friday's data are weak, we may see yields falling further throughout the curve, as liquidity has loosened throughout the curve."  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires, 65-6415-4118, weiyi.lim@dowjones.com [ 01-11-06 0722GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061101e2b1000d6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
