\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down On Short-Covering,Rumored  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2006\par 07:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                        Latest   Change \par  USD/SGD               1.5618   +0.0013 \par  Overnight Rate        3.62%    +6 bps \par  2 Year Bond Yield     3.01%    -1 bps \par  10-Year Bond Yield    3.18%    - \par  2-Year Swap Offer     3.52%    +1 bps \par  10-Year Swap Offer    3.63%    +1 bps \par  2-10-Year Swap Curve  11 bps   - \par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Dow Jones)--Speculation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and dollar short-covering dragged the Singapore dollar lower Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "There was talk of the MAS in the market at different levels," said one local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS' key monetary policy tool is to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 "There shouldn't be any significant downside in the pair (in the near term)," said Jimmy Koh, head of treasury research at United Overseas Bank. "According to my estimation of the band, the pair is already 2.26% stronger than the midpoint. The MAS normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it is 2.1% above the midpoint."  \par \par \uc2 Koh also predicted that the greenback would be supported at S$1.5580, unless the USD/JPY falls below Y116.50.  \par \par \uc2 Another local bank dealer said that the U.S. dollar is "still heavy" and that will only change if October U.S. nonfarm payrolls data due Friday is stronger than expected.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore bond market, prices were almost unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 "There was some rally in the three- to four-year bonds on customers' purchases," said a local bank dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "With no new issuances locally, we can only track U.S. data," he said. "Expect volatility as there are a lot of U.S. data, starting tonight."  \par \par \uc2 October's US Chicago Purchasing Managers Index will be released at 1500 GMT. If U.S. data is stronger than expected, bond prices will likely fall.  \par \par \uc2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires, 65-6415-4118, weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 31-10-06 0603GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061031e2av000ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
