\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -At multi-week highs, Thai c.bank steps in  \b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2006\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to multi-week highs against the dollar on Friday, propped up by foreign investment inflows, the Chinese yuan's steady rise and the weakness in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan's <CNY=CXFS> rise to 7.8870 per dollar, its highest level since its revaluation in July 2005, helped boost Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the board.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose to 1.5650 per U.S. dollar, a 5-month peak, with the market wary of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders said the MAS had been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "But the market is still looking to buy the Singapore dollar, presumably still taking the unit as a proxy to yuan views. The Sing dollar has remained as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the highest correlation and beta to the yuan," analysts at UBS said in a note to clients.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> climbed to 36.84 to the U.S. dollar, its strongest level since January 2000, while the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> rose as far as 9,075 per U.S. dollar, its strongest since Sept. 6.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand has received a net $446 million worth of net foreign portfolio investments so far this month, stock exchange data showed, taking total net investments this year to more than $3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may raise the limits on offshore investment to ease pressure on the baht. She had warned markets earlier this week that the baht's rise had been too rapid.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's broad weakness underpinned regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was under pressure as the market priced in expectations the Fed would continue to keep rates on hold after it kept them steady this week for a third straight meeting.  \par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> was quoted at a seven-week high of 3.6480 per dollar, propped up by foreign inflows into Malaysian assets. The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a one-month high.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said portfolio investments into Asia could increase after Chinese lender Industrial & Commercial Bank of China's solid trading debut on Friday following its record US$19 billion IPO.  \par \par \uc2 "It's blue sky ahead for risky assets. What's driving the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is confidence-sensitive portfolio flows into regional equity markets," said Tim Condon, ING Bank's regional economist and strategist.  \par \par \uc2 "The trend is your friend in this case," he said, adding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to appreciate until the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the yen <JPY=> lagged the rise in most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after softer-than-expected Japanese inflation data. It rallied to levels around 118.50 per dollar from 118.74 late in Asian trade the previous session but hit a record low against the euro <EURJPY=>. Japan's core consumer price index in September climbed 0.2 percent from a year earlier, lower than forecasts, sparking expectations that the Bank of Japan could wait until 2007 to raise interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The weakness in the yen was a hurdle for the rallying Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "The story in Japan is capital outflows, given the outlook for the economy as well as financial policies are very supportive of dollar/yen," Condon said.  \par \par \uc2 "So it will be difficult for this appreciation of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to become a real strong trend, given the headwind of well supported dollar/yen," he said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0806 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.53         118.74       +0.18\par  Sing dlr        1.5653         1.5702       +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr      33.280         33.262       -0.05\par  Korean won      947.20         949.60       +0.25\par  Baht             36.88          37.00       +0.33\par  Peso             49.80          49.87       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9100.00        9112.00       +0.13\par  Rupee            45.19          45.26       +0.17\par  Ringgit         3.6480         3.6640       +0.44\par  Yuan            7.8911         7.8948       +0.05\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.53         117.96       -0.48\par  Sing dlr        1.5653         1.6625       +6.21\par  Taiwan dlr      33.280         32.850       -1.29\par  Korean won      947.20        1011.60       +6.80\par  Baht             36.88          41.11      +11.47\par  Peso             49.80          53.09       +6.61\par  Rupiah         9100.00        9835.00       +8.08\par  Rupee            45.19          45.04       -0.32\par  Ringgit         3.6480         3.7790       +3.59\par  Yuan            7.8911         8.0702       +2.27\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J