\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Thai baht off highs, Sing dlr supported  \b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2006\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 25 (Reuters) - Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Thailand reined in the Thai baht on Wednesday after foreign investment flows boosted it to its strongest level in nearly seven years, close to 37 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> was underpinned by flows from funds betting on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, pushing it to what analysts said was the top of the secret trade-weighted band within which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore manages it.  \par \par \uc2 Markets in Indonesia and Malaysia were closed but other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed, shrugging off the yen's weakness as foreign investment flowed into the region. The South Korean won <KRW=> rose 0.4 percent to around 955 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Southeast Asian stock markets have been the bigger beneficiaries of foreign investment flows, with the Hong Kong and Indonesian markets near recent highs and Singapore's Straits Times Index <.STI> hitting a record high on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> remained in a 119.10-119.20 per dollar range as nervousness ahead of a Federal Reserve policy decision trapped the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed's two-day policy meeting ends on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Economists expect U.S. rates to be left unchanged this week. The Fed raised rates 17 times in two years up to June, but kept them steady in August and September.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose a quarter of a percent to 1.5721 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Much of the flow pressure seems to be coming from models, which presumably are rebuilding positions they had closed in the run-up to this month's policy review," said Mirza Baig, Deutsche Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar was sought by funds that mainly use trends to trade \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Singapore dollar is the most liquid emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, he said.  \par \par \uc2 BAHT GAINS HALTED  \par \par \uc2 The baht was quoted as high as 37.06 per dollar, its highest level since January 2000, but retreated somewhat after new Bank of Thailand Governor Tarisa Watanagase said it was rising too fast.  \par \par \uc2 The baht has gained 1.3 percent in two weeks. Some dealers had expected the baht to weaken in anticipation of a possible sale by Singapore state firm Temasek Holdings [TEM.UL] of a stake in Thailand's Shin Corp , which it bought in January from the family of ousted Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra.  \par \par \uc2 Thaksin's critics have said the agreement breached foreign ownership laws and the deal is under investigation.  \par \par \uc2 "I am sceptical about that flow rumour," said Claudio Piron, a JPMorgan Chase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.  \par \par \uc2 "We are relatively optimistic on baht partly because we feel there is some undervaluation in the assets and partly because, with the prospect of political stabilisation, we could be getting investment picking up," Piron said.  \par \par \uc2 "And foreign equity purchases have been very strong relative to the rest of the region."  \par \par \uc2 Data from the stock exchange showed net foreign portfolio inflows into Thailand have been about $389 million so far in October.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand's 242-member National Legislative Assembly, handpicked by the leaders of the military coup, met for the first time on Tuesday. The baht has now fully recovered losses made after the Sept. 19 military coup. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0831 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.15         118.96       -0.16\par  Sing dlr        1.5722         1.5750       +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr      33.310         33.267       -0.13\par  Korean won      955.70         959.30       +0.38\par  Baht             37.11          37.20       +0.24\par  Peso             49.93          50.06       +0.26\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9150.00       +0.38\par  Rupee            45.35          45.39       +0.09\par  Ringgit         3.6740         3.6740       +0.00\par  Yuan            7.8985         7.8990       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.15         117.96       -1.00\par  Sing dlr        1.5722         1.6625       +5.74\par  Taiwan dlr      33.310         32.850       -1.38\par  Korean won      955.70        1011.60       +5.85\par  Baht             37.11          41.11      +10.78\par  Peso             49.93          53.09       +6.33\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9835.00       +7.90\par  Rupee            45.35          45.04       -0.68\par  Ringgit         3.6740         3.7790       +2.86\par  Yuan            7.8985         8.0702       +2.17\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061028e2ap000ei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
