\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Touch lower on yen weakness  \b0\par\par\uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2006\par 04:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 19 (Reuters) - A softer tone in the yen pushed most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down on Thursday, but trade was generally subdued as the market waited for fresh direction.  \par \par \uc2 A degree of caution also lingered amid concerns about North Korea following last week's nuclear test.  \par \par \uc2 The yen shed about 0.4 percent to around 119 per dollar <JPY=>, but had trimmed some of its falls by late trade.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> eased to about 958 per dollar, down 0.6 percent from this week's one-week highs, while the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> dipped to about 33.23 to the U.S. dollar -- heading back towards last week's 10-month low at 33.34.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> slipped to about 37.40 per dollar, down a quarter of a percent from Wednesday's one-month high at about 37.30, although the Singapore dollar <SGD=> touched a fresh 5-1/2-week high at about 1.5735.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. data on Wednesday was mixed, while reports this week that Russia has started to buy the yen for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and the Bank of Japan plans to increase its monitoring of carry trades appear to have given the yen only a modest boost.  \par \par \uc2 "In the last few weeks, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have done reasonably well and risk appetite has rebounded," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But we are still stuck in a range and we still need to see a clear trend in the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 Henderson said that in the current environment the appeal of trading Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against each other instead of versus the dollar had risen.  \par \par \uc2 "The Philippine peso, for instance, has outperformed the Sing dollar and the won," he said. "The crosses are where the opportunities are."  \par \par \uc2 WATCHING THE FLOWS  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the Singapore dollar probably remained at the strong end of its undisclosed trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb strength in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given slight yen weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Markets had been wary of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar rallied.  \par \par \uc2 There was some talk that the gains were related to Singapore state investment firm Temasek [TEM.UL] selling share holdings in Thai telecommunications group Shin Corp to resolve a foreign ownership dispute.  \par \par \uc2 IDEAglobal analysts said the deal could potentially see flows of as much as $1.5 billion, with the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely to benefit if the proceeds are converted back to \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is not particularly worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment as the yen is staying here," said the trader.  \par \par \uc2 "The Temasek news has been digested and yesterday the sell-off in dollar/Sing was by model funds, and more speculative or long liquidation."  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> rose a fifth of a percent to about 3.6680 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It continues to draw support from cash flows into Malaysia related to the acquisition of about $2 billion of Malaysian OYL Industries Bhd by Japanese air-conditioner maker Daikin Industries Ltd. , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed little reaction to Chinese data.  \par \par \uc2 China's annual economic growth slowed a little in the third quarter to 10.4 percent, from 11.3 percent in the second quarter.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0734 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.65         118.55       -0.08\par  Sing dlr        1.5736         1.5751       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      33.213         33.180       -0.10\par  Korean won      957.10         955.40       -0.18\par  Baht             37.33          37.32       -0.03\par  Peso             50.00          49.93       -0.14\par  Rupiah         9153.00        9150.00       -0.03\par  Rupee            45.29          45.38       +0.19\par  Ringgit         3.6690         3.6755       +0.18\par  Yuan            7.9096         7.9072       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.65         117.96       -0.58\par  Sing dlr        1.5736         1.6625       +5.65\par  Taiwan dlr      33.213         32.850       -1.09\par  Korean won      957.10        1011.60       +5.69\par  Baht             37.33          41.11      +10.13\par  Peso             50.00          53.09       +6.18\par  Rupiah         9153.00        9835.00       +7.45\par  Rupee            45.29          45.04       -0.55\par  Ringgit         3.6690         3.7790       +3.00\par  Yuan            7.9096         8.0702       +2.03\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 