\par\par \b \uc2 DATA VIEW: Singapore Inflation At 11-Month Low In Aug  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Jannarone  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2006\par 09:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Singapore's inflation rate slipped below the government's targeted range in August, but economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its modestly tight monetary stance when policy is reviewed in October.  \par \par \uc2 The consumer price index rose just 0.7% from a year earlier in August, the slowest pace since September 2005, according to official figures released Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has a target range for inflation of 1% to 2% for 2006, and has said it expects inflation in the bottom of the same range in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 Seasonally-adjusted, the consumer price index remained unchanged from July.  \par \par \uc2 August's data was below the average of a Dow Jones Newswires poll, which forecasted the CPI would rise by 1.0% from a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 David Cohen, an economist at Action Economics, said prices are not at a great risk of rising or falling too quickly, and that current inflation levels are unlikely to motivate a change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy stance.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think there's any hurry to shift from the slightly appreciating band," Cohen said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore advocates a modest and gradual appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the local dollar within an undisclosed, trade-weighted band.  \par \par \uc2 Some market players have speculated that benign inflation would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Singapore dollar, but economists say the current policy allows sufficient room for fluctuation.  \par \par \uc2 "The band is already quite flexible," said Sim Moh Siong, economist at Citigroup.  \par \par \uc2 Sim said that an overly-strong Singapore dollar could be a liability in the event of a recession, but such a scenario is unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 "We are in the soft-landing camp," Sim said. "We are not looking at a 2001 scenario. U.S. growth should still be 3% next year."  \par \par \uc2 Since the beginning of 2006, the Singapore dollar has appreciated by about 5% against the U.S. dollar, which began the year around S$1.6620 and is currently at S$1.5840.  \par \par \uc2 The stronger Singapore dollar has helped shield Singapore against external price pressure.  \par \par \uc2 DBS strategist Philip Wee said that lower oil prices have eased external pressures further.  \par \par \uc2 After reaching a high of around $78 dollars this summer, Nymex crude is currently trading around $60 per barrel.  \par \par \uc2 Wee said that domestic inflation is also "quite benign" because of subdued wage pressure and a decline in the cost for Certificates of Entitlement, which allow Singaporeans to own cars.  \par \par \uc2 He said COE prices declined ahead of the August CPI sampling, which accounts for much of the decline in transportation costs.  \par \par \uc2 The cost of transport and communication, which represents 22% of the inflation index, fell 1.8% from a year earlier in August and fell 0.1% from July.  \par \par \uc2 Among other key components, housing costs, which make up 21% of the index, rose 2.1% in August from a year earlier, but fell 0.1% from July.  \par \par \uc2 The cost of food, which makes up 23% of the index, rose 1.7% from a year earlier and remained unchanged from July.  \par \par \uc2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Stephen Wright [ 25-09-06 0750GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060925e29p000cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
