\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down As MAS Action Expected; Bonds Stable  \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2006\par 10:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was weaker in Asian trade Tuesday on expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been trading at the strong end of its policy band.  \par \par \uc2 A local bank dealer said his bank estimated that the Singapore dollar was just shy of 2% above the center of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS operates monetary policy by managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band rather than using interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 A foreign bank dealer said the IMF and World Bank meeting this week in Singapore is "still the focus. But it has yet to release any major news."  \par \par \uc2 Emmanuel Ng, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist from the Overseas Chinese Banking Corp., said market players would also be looking overseas for cues.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is a removal of reference on deflation in the Japanese Cabinet Office economic report this Friday, the Japanese yen will get support," Ng said. "There is also the U.S. trade deficit numbers tonight."  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar tracks the yen closely.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. July trade deficit data will be released later in the global session. A survey by Dow Jones Newswires predicts the deficit at US$64.5 billion, compared with US$64.8 billion in June.  \par \par \uc2 At 0655 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.5787, up from S$1.5767 at New York close and S$1.5744 in late Asian trade Monday.  \par \par \uc2 In the government debt market, the two-year bond yield remained flat at 3.03%, while the 10-year bond yield rose one basis point to 3.33%.  \par \par \uc2 "The bonds are holding steady," a local dealer said. "There is a little shedding of the prices."  \par \par \uc2 "It's a quiet market today, but the market is a little nervous, as the U.S. Treasurys are trading lower," the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest  Previous \par Overnight rate        2.69%    2.69% \par Two-year bond yield:  3.03%    3.03% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.33%    3.32% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.54%    3.54% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.68%    3.68% \par 2-10-yr swap curve:   14bps    14bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires, 65-6415-4118, weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 12-09-06 0802GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060912e29c000c2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
