 at New York close and S$1.5744 in late Asian trade Monday. \par \par   In the government debt market, the two-year bond yield remained flat at 3.03%, while the 10-year bond yield rose one basis point to 3.33%.\par  \par   'The bonds are holding steady,' a local dealer said. 'There is a little shedding of the prices.' \par \par    'It's a quiet market today, but the market is a little nervous, as the U.S. Treasurys are trading lower,' the trader said. \par \par                       Latest  Previous \par Overnight rate        2.69%    2.69% \par Two-year bond yield:  3.03%    3.03% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.33%    3.32% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.54%    3.54% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.68%    3.68% \par 2-10-yr swap curve:   14bps    14bps \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires, 65-6415-4118, weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -Edited by Graham Norris -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060912e29c004k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
