\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen lends support, spotlight on G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2006\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 8 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held steady on Friday, supported by a rally in the yen after a German finance official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness would be a topic at this month's Group of Seven meeting.  \par \par \uc2 The yen hit one-month highs against the euro <EURJPY=R> and rose to about 116.10 per U.S. dollar <JPY=>, up about 0.7 percent from late on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 A firmer yen helped push the South Korean won <KRW=> briefly to about 954 per dollar, the strongest level since the end of July, while the Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose to 1.5657 per U.S. dollar overnight -- its highest since mid-May.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers suspected that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore stepped into the market to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains in overnight trade and wariness of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action kept the market in a tight range on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks like there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, but not so far today," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. "People seem to be paying full attention to any comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it looks like this will be a big issue during the G7 and IMF meetings."  \par \par \uc2 Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from the G7 industrial nations will meet on Sept. 16 in Singapore, Japan's Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Friday. Singapore, China and Thailand have been invited to join part of the discussions.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be discussed but declined to say if the yen would be at the centre of such talks.  \par \par \uc2 As most traders had been expecting the Chinese yuan and not the yen to be a key focus, Thursday's comments by German Deputy Finance Minister Thomas Mirow came as a surprise and prompted short covering of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Yesterday's comments from the German Deputy Finance Minister woke the market up to the risks that there could be major fireworks at this G7 meeting," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered. "Today's comments confirm that the focus is very much on the need for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate. Asia has to play its part."  \par \par \uc2 Henderson added that the move in the euro to almost 150 yen has encouraged European officials to suggest that Asia should take up more of the burden of reducing global imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Friday, however, that he did not expect the yen to be the centre of the G7 finance ministers' discussions.  \par \par \uc2 YUAN IN SPOTLIGHT TOO  \par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> was also in the spotlight ahead of this month's meetings of the G7 and International Monetary Fund, with markets digesting a raft of comments from officials on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 China rejected blame for global economic imbalances, while U.S. Treasury Secretary Henry Paulson said that the United States and China agree \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility is "very important."  \par \par \uc2 The official Financial News, meanwhile, said China may widen the yuan's trading band against the dollar to allow greater fluctuation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Recent volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested Beijing may make such a move, the paper said, without giving a timeframe.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan has risen about 0.8 percent in the past three weeks to hit 7.9367 per dollar on Tuesday, its highest level since it was revalued by 2.1 percent in July 2005. Some analysts say a widening of the yuan's trading band is likely to happen soon.  \par \par \uc2 "The political mileage that the Chinese can gain from widening the band ahead of the (G7) summit is a powerful incentive to act early," said Deutsche Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mirza Baig. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change of the day at 0740 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.26         116.91       +0.56\par  Sing dlr        1.5696         1.5685       -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      32.876         32.860       -0.05\par  Korean won      956.20         956.40       +0.02\par  Baht             37.38          37.42       +0.11\par  Peso             50.50          50.50       +0.01\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9098.00       -0.19\par  Rupee            46.24          46.22       -0.03\par  Ringgit         3.6550         3.6500       -0.14\par  Yuan            7.9500         7.9395       -0.13\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.26         117.96       +1.46\par  Sing dlr        1.5696         1.6625       +5.92\par  Taiwan dlr      32.876         32.850       -0.08\par  Korean won      956.20        1011.60       +5.79\par  Baht             37.38          41.11       +9.98\par  Peso             50.50          53.09       +5.14\par  Rupiah         9115.00        9835.00       +7.90\par  Rupee            46.24          45.04       -2.58\par  Ringgit         3.6550         3.7790       +3.3