\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dlr at 3-\u189\'00\'BD   month high, mkt wary of MAS  \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2006\par 03:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 4 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar rose to its highest level in about 3-\u189\'00\'BD   months versus a generally soft U.S. dollar on Monday, after breaking through key chart levels.  \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that with the Singapore dollar <SGD=> most probably trading at the strong end of its secret trade-weighted band, they were wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) in the market to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar strengthened as far as 1.5665 per U.S. dollar, its strongest since about mid-May and up about a third of a percent from levels traded late on Friday.  \par \par \uc2  "Local banks have been selling dollar/Sing and the move through 1.57 triggered a wave of stop-loss selling," said a trader in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2  "So far we have not seen any signs of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but if dollar/Sing continues to drift lower, they (the MAS) are likely to come in."  \par \par \uc2  Traders said the absence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in recent weeks has encouraged investors to push the Singapore dollar higher.     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060904e2940002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
