\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Touch firmer, fresh 4-year highs for peso  \b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2006\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 1 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a touch firmer ahead of key U.S. jobs numbers due later on Friday, with the Philippine peso extending this week's rally to hit a four-year peak against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> rose as far as 50.70 per U.S. dollar, taking its gains this week to about 1.2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Strong foreign demand for local bonds and stocks, remittances from overseas workers, an easing of political worries and upbeat economic data have all been pushing the peso higher.  \par \par \uc2 But after a week of gains, the peso rally was starting to run out of steam, dealers said. "Dollar/peso has been oversold in the last few days so it is time for a pause and there was bit of profit taking around 50.70," said a trader in Manila.  \par \par \uc2 He said it was not clear if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to curb peso strength.  \par \par \uc2 "The peso is moving in accordance with the market," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Amando Tetangco said on Friday. "Good economic data continues to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . What we would rather not see is too much volatility."  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> was stuck in a tight 9,095 to 9,089 per dollar range.  \par \par \uc2 It drew some support from data showing Indonesia's annual consumer inflation rate fell to 14.9 percent in August, its lowest level since last September.  \par \par \uc2 Data showing a stronger-than-expected 18.7 percent rise in South Korean exports in August underpinned the won <KRW=> around 959 per dollar, the intraday high.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> firmed slightly to about 32.87 per U.S. dollar as a rally in local equities <.TWII> lifted expectations of foreign fund inflows.  \par \par \uc2 PAYROLLS EYED  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. August non-farm payrolls report is due at 1230 GMT and economists polled by Reuters forecast a median 120,000 new jobs were created compared with 113,000 in July.  \par \par \uc2 "Over the last three weeks the focus has shifted to the risks to growth from the risks to inflation," said Jimmy Koh, head of economics and treasury at United Overseas Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The payrolls should give us a good sense of how much of a moderation in growth to expect."  \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> hit 7.9525 per dollar, matching a post-revaluation high set on Thursday, before profit taking pulled the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on the day.  \par \par \uc2 Yuan strength this week has helped offset the impact of yen weakness on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The yen, which often sets the regional tone, hit a record low against the euro <EURJPY=> and six-week lows against the dollar <JPY=> on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "A different dynamic seems to be driving Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it appears to be linked much more strongly to the yuan," said RBC Capital Markets senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sue Trinh.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers watched the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=> for signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS). The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was estimated to be at the strong end of its trading band, partly because of strength against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "My estimates are that the Singapore dollar is trading 1.5 percent above the mid-point of the band," said Trinh.  \par \par \uc2 "That is somewhat surprising and there is a fair amount of concern that the MAS might come in to prevent further gains in the Sing dollar, which is preventing U.S. dollar/Sing dollar from trading too much below 1.57." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0832 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.31         117.25       -0.05\par  Sing dlr        1.5715         1.5712       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      32.881         32.906       +0.08\par  Korean won      960.40         961.40       +0.10\par  Baht             37.51          37.56       +0.14\par  Peso             50.66          50.80       +0.28\par  Rupiah         9093.00        9100.00       +0.08\par  Rupee            46.53          46.51       -0.05\par  Ringgit         3.6710         3.6800       +0.25\par  Yuan            7.9543         7.9530       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.31         117.96       +0.55\par  Sing dlr        1.5715         1.6625       +5.79\par  Taiwan dlr      32.881         32.850       -0.09\par  Korean won      960.40        1011.60       +5.33\par  Baht             37.51          41.11       +9.60\par  Peso             50.66          53.09       +4.80\par  Rupiah         9093.00        9835.00       +8.16\par  Rupee            46.53          45.04       -3.21\par  Ringgit         3.6710         3.7790       +2.94\par  Yuan            7.9543         8.0702       +1.46\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060904e