\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Hits  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Policy Ceiling; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2006\par 10:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar edged higher in Asian trade Friday but encountered resistance as it reached the strong end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone wants to be short the (U.S.) dollar against Asia, but the Singapore dollar basket is trading at the high end of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range," a dealer at a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore manages the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an unspecified band, and market players say the MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to stem gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "MAS came in to bring (the U.S. dollar) back up to the S$1.5715-S$1.5720 level," the dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0636 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.5722, from S$1.5732 at the close of New York trade and S$1.5717 in late Asian trade Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Some players use the relatively liquid Singapore dollar to take on exposure to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which many believe have the potential to gain against the U.S. dollar in the coming months.  \par \par \uc2 "Only Asia has been lacking against the U.S. dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from other regions - like the euro, British pound and Australian dollar - have already gained quite a bit," said Emmanuel Ng, a strategist at OCBC bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The big picture is that the market expects some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, and the Singapore dollar also reflects strength in (the Chinese yuan)," Ng said.  \par \par \uc2 But some analysts think the Singapore dollar has already traded outside of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target band for the last few sessions, and some players may take short positions as they perceive upside risk to be minimal.  \par \par \uc2 "Gains are seen as limited for the Singapore dollar, so it is a good funding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a carry trade with the Indonesian rupiah or Philippine peso, which have higher interest rates," a local dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Investors can benefit from interest rate differentials by taking loans in Singapore dollars and buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that offer higher rates of interest on deposits.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the U.S. dollar to be supported at S$1.5680 and face resistance at S$1.5750 next week.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore government debt market, longer-dated issues posted significant gains after an overnight rally brought yields on U.S. 10-year Treasury notes to a five-month low.  \par \par \uc2 "The three or four basis-point fall in yields was a catch-up from earlier this week," a local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday and Thursday, Singapore government bonds held steady, despite gains in U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year Singapore government bond bid-side yield was one basis point lower at 3.13%, while the 10- and 15-year bid-side yields each fell four basis points to 3.36% and 3.43%, respectively.  \par \par \uc2 "The overnight rate is still high, so the market was buying the long end of the curve to avoid negative carry," another trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Recently, short-dated bond yields have fallen beneath the overnight rate.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say the timing of a possible interest rate cut in the U.S. is the bond market's key focus in coming weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The release of the U.S. August nonfarm payroll figure, slated for tonight, may give an indication of whether the U.S. economy is cooling, and how soon the Fed may cut rates.  \par \par \uc2 "Payrolls will be the main focus into next week," a local trader said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest  Previous \par Overnight rate        3.13%   3.25% \par Two-year bond yield:  3.13%   3.14% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.36%   3.40% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.56%   3.57% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.67%   3.69% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  11bps   12bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 01-09-06 0816GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060901e291000dj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
