\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Edges Up;Resistance Seen At Top Of MAS Band  \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2006\par 10:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar gained slightly in Asian trade Thursday but was restrained by market perceptions that it was strengthening beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range.  \par \par \uc2 "The one key factor keeping the Singapore dollar from moving higher is that current levels put it at the top end of the trading band," said UBS \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Nizam Idris.  \par \par \uc2 At 0755 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.5717, down from S$1.5736 at the close of New York trade and S$1.5727 in late Asian trade Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore manages the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an unspecified band. The MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, and financial analysts make calculations on the trading levels that might prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action.  \par \par \uc2 "The trade-weighted index is at its strongest point since the last policy meeting in April," said Irene Cheung, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 Weakness in the Japanese yen also likely contained the rise of the Singapore dollar, and some analysts say there is downside risk for both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen weakens further.  \par \par \uc2 "If (the U.S. dollar) breaks out to the upside through Y117.50, there could be a big move further, even though the market is already very short yen," said ABN's Cheung. "And if there is a breakout, we could see some retracement in the Singapore dollar."  \par \par \uc2 The yen declined Thursday morning in Asia on weaker-than-expected Japanese industrial output data that suggested the Bank of Japan might not raise rates again this year.  \par \par \uc2 At 0755 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at Y117.25, compared with Y117.08 at the beginning of Asian trade.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has weakened recently as prospects for higher rates in other economies weigh against Japan's rates, which are likely to stay low.  \par \par \uc2 ABN's Cheung notes there is a 417-basis-point spread between the two-year U.S. Treasury yield and the two-year Japanese Government Bond yield, the largest since July.  \par \par \uc2 Traders expect the U.S. dollar to be supported at S$1.5700 and face resistance at S$1.5770 in the next few days.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore government debt market, a modest bid for mid-dated maturities reflected demand for U.S. Treasurys overnight, when the market showed healthy appetite in an auction for new five-year Treasury notes.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year Singapore government bond yield was flat at 3.14%, while the five- and seven-year yields each fell one basis point to 3.27% and 3.31%, respectively. The 10-year yield was flat at 3.40%, as was the 15-year yield at 3.47%.  \par \par \uc2 "The five-year was catching up after the 15-year rallied earlier in the week," a local trader said. "There was a lot of flattening on the five- to 15-year curve and it is correcting."  \par \par \uc2 At a reopening of the 15-year Singapore government bond Tuesday, the auction closed at a cutoff yield of 3.48%, below the 3.50%-3.60% some had expected.  \par \par \uc2 Players in the Singapore bond market will watch for signs of inflation in economic data releases from the U.S. this week, especially the personal spending data due later Thursday, and nonfarm payrolls due Friday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest  Previous \par Overnight rate        3.25%   3.25% \par Two-year bond yield:  3.14%   3.14% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.40%   3.40% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.57%   3.62% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.69%   3.75% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  12bps   13bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By John Jannarone, Dow Jones Newswires; 65 6415 4152; john.jannarone@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 31-08-06 0851GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060831e28v000lq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
