\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Gains Slightly On US Data; Bonds Up  \b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2006\par 10:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose for the third consecutive session in Asian trade Monday after weaker-than-forecast U.S. nonfarm payrolls raised expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will take a break from raising interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 'The U.S. dollar dropped too fast this morning,' said Suan Teck Kim, an economist with United Overseas Bank. 'Thus, there could be a possible rebound of the U.S. dollar tomorrow, even if the Fed paused the rate hike' cycle at its meeting Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 At 0638 GMT, the U.S. unit was trading at $1.5713, down from S$1.5731 at the New York close and $1.5770 late Friday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell against the Singapore dollar due to the payrolls data released Friday in the U.S.  \par \par \uc2 Nonfarm payrolls grew 113,000 in July, less than the predicted 150,000 increase, adding weight to the view that the Fed will leave rates unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 Further gains in the Singapore dollar could be capped by fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.  \par \par \uc2 'There is the fear of the MAS to keep the Singapore dollar in check,' Suan said.  \par \par \uc2 Some 22 of 23 primary dealers polled by Dow Jones Newswires and CNBC believe the Fed will keep its overnight target rate fixed at 5.25%.  \par \par \uc2 'The effect of a pause in the rate hike is already priced in,' a trader from a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 'So the pause in the rate hike is unlikely to change the U.S. dollar drastically tomorrow. Rather, we are more concerned about the statement to check for clues for future rate hikes.'  \par \par \uc2 Suan said that the U.S. dollar is likely to remain in the S$1.5700-S$1.5800 range.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore government debt market, the two-year bond yield fell one basis point to 2.97%, while the 10-year yield fell five basis points to 3.43%.  \par \par \uc2 'The Singapore bonds rallied because of the weak nonfarm payrolls in the morning and rose by five basis points across the board,' a local bank dealer said.'  \par \par \uc2 'During lunch, the cutoff yield of the three-month (treasury bill) tender was much higher than expected, so there was a lot of selling in the short end. In the end, the shorter-dated bonds remained unchanged.'  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said the market had expected the treasury bills to be sold at a yield of 2.93% or below compared with the 3.00% they were actually sold for in the auction.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Latest  Previous \par  Overnight rate        2.63%   2.6388% \par  Two-year bond yield:  2.97%   2.98% \par  10-year bond yield:   3.43%   3.48% \par  Two-year swap offer:  3.64%   3.70% \par  10-year swap offer:   3.84%   3.89% \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2-10-yr swap spread: 20 bps 19 bps Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\uc2 \f2  -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4118; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com -Edited by Mary de Wet -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060807e2870048v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
