\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Up On Casino Inflow Talk;Bond Curve Steeper  \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2006\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose late Wednesday in Asian trade on continued expectation of remittances linked to Singapore's first casino project.  \par \par \uc2 "The Singapore dollar is strengthening, as the market is still speculating that the Las Vegas Sands Corp. (LVS) is going to remit \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Singapore within these few days," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 In late May, Singapore named Sands the winning bidder for the casino project. Sands will have to pay the Singapore government about US$750 million before the end of August to cover the cost of the waterfront site at Marina Bay as well as various taxes.  \par \par \uc2 At 0616 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.5905, down from S$1.5929 in New York and S$1.5925 late Monday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback is well supported at the S$1.5900 level, another trader said. The U.S. dollar reached an intraday low at S$1.5888 around 0200 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a possibility that the MAS (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the greenback from falling further, but I doubt they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  that greatly as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is within range" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy trading band, the second trader said.  \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, government bond prices were mixed, with prices falling in the longer end, further steepening the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year bond yield remained unchanged at 2.94%, while the 10-year bond yield gained four basis points to 3.55%, steepening the curve.  \par \par \uc2 "The bond market will remain rangebound until the government seven-year bond auction announcement later today," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is expected to announce the auction size of the seven-year paper later in the Asian day, with market participants expecting the amount to be between S$1 billion and S$1.3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest  Previous \par Overnight Rate        3.625%  3.250% \par Two-year bond yield:  2.94%   2.94% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.55%   3.51% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.66%   3.66% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.87%   3.87% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  21 bps  21 bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Wei Yi Lim, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4118; weiyi.lim@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 21-06-06 0634GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060621e26l00081\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
