\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Gains On Hopes Of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Inflows; Bonds Weak  \b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2006\par 10:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar gained Monday on expectations of more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows linked to a new casino project, as well as mergers and acquisition activity in the city-state.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were weaker and the curve flatter, but trading volumes remained thin even after an auction for five-year bonds, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0646 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.5788, below S$1.5802 at the close of the New York session. In Asian trade late Friday, the greenback was at S$1.5800.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar opened on a weak note against the local unit on last Friday's announcement that Las Vegas Sands' S$5 billion proposal made them the successful bidder for Singapore's first casino and integrated resort project.  \par \par \uc2 The US-based casino giant has to pay S$1.2 billion within the coming weeks, which the market saw as an opportunity to sell the greenback, a local bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The selling in the U.S. dollar came despite early gains against the yen which failed to spillover into the Singapore market, as investors had positioned themselves for more gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The local unit was also helped by news that Indonesia's Lippo is buying a 55.04% stake in Overseas Union Enterprise from Singapore's second biggest bank, United Overseas Bank (U11.SG), and three associated companies for S$989.9 million in cash, triggering a takeover offer for OUE.  \par \par \uc2 However thin volumes due in part to a U.S. holiday Monday prevented larger gains, they said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    United Overseas Bank said in a research note that the short-term downside for the U.S. dollar was capped at S$1.5750, considering an absence of direction from regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and recent sharp gains in the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted exchange rate. \par   A huge rise in the rate, which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't disclose, risks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in favor of the U.S. dollar, since it counters its current policy of allowing only modest and gradual gains in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par   In the bond market, the two-year yield rose by four basis point to 2.90% in thin, cautious trade ahead of the U.S. holiday. The 10-year yield rose one basis point to 3.49%. \par   However after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's auction for five-year bond met market expectations, trading remained lackluster, traders said. \par   The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold S$1.1 billion in five-year bonds at 3.27%, in line with market expectations of 3.25%-3.30%, dealers said. \par   The market is looking for excuse to buy at the shorter end of the curve and waiting for clues on when the Federal Reserve may end its tightening policy, dealers said. \par   The near-term trend for the curve is to steepen, led by a fall in short-term yields, a local bank dealer said. \par                      Latest  Previous \par Overnight Rate        2.81%   2.93% \par Two-year bond yield:  2.90%   2.86% \par 10-year bond yield:   3.49%   3.48% \par Two-year swap offer:  3.55%   3.56% \par 10-year swap offer:   3.80%   3.80% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  25 bps  24 bps \par   Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Michael Kitchen -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060529e25t004s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
