\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Slightly Up; Bonds Gain On Local Buying  \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2006\par 10:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose slightly in Asia Friday, tracking early weakness in the U.S. dollar, but more gains were capped by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rallied, led by local buying in the 10-year paper, which unexpectedly flattened the yield curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0659 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.5980, compared with S$1.5985 at the close of New York trade. In late Asian trade Thursday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.5981.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar traded in a range of S$1.5974 and S$1.6002.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said trading was lackluster as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked the U.S. dollar's movement against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 After slipping to Y117.38 early, the U.S. dollar stabilized to Y117.61 in afternoon trade, little changed from the New York close.  \par \par \uc2 Comments by Singapore's trade minister about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also failed to move the market.  \par \par \uc2 "The adjustment in the Singapore dollar is due to market forces, and it also reflects the strength of the Singapore economy," Trade and Industry Minister Lim Hng Kiang told reporters Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar is near an eight-year high and has risen 6.6% since late November when the rally began.  \par \par \uc2 Recent suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been preventing a decline in the U.S. dollar after it recovered from Thursday's intraday low of S$1.5959 - the lowest in eight years.  \par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas said in a note the U.S. dollar should find support at S$1.5973 and resistance at S$1.6007.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year bond yield slipped four basis points to 3.49%, while the 10-year interest-rate swap rate briefly dropped below 3.90% from a peak of 3.97% Thursday, after a local bank stepped up buying to adjust positions, said a dealer.  \par \par \uc2 The gains were unexpected after U.S. Treasurys fell overnight and traded flat in Tokyo trade Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year yield slipped one basis point to 3.08%, flattening the curve by three basis points to 41 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest  Previous \par Overnight Rate       2.813%   2.750% \par Two-year bond yield  3.08%    3.09% \par 10-year bond yield   3.49%    3.53% \par Two-year swap offer  3.54%    3.60% \par 10-year swap offer   3.90%    3.97% \par 2-10-yr swap spread: 36 bps   37 bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Graham Norris [ 21-04-06 0811GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060421e24l000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
