\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Hu's visit disappoints, rupiah supported  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan  \par \uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2006\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, April 21 (Reuters) - China's yuan slipped in offshore forwards on Friday and some Asian regionals fell after being sold by speculators disappointed with Chinese President Hu Jintao's comments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his U.S. visit.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> fell a quarter of a percent and the Philippine peso <PHP=> hit a 1-\u189\'00\'BD month trough of 51.71 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, South Korean won <KRW=> and Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> were supported by foreign investment inflows. The won <KRW=> rose to about 946 per dollar, just shy of the 8-1/2-year peak of 944 struck on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "It is a disappointment, undoubtedly. The easiest thing would have been for dollar/China to have made it below 8 and it could not even do that," said Claudio Piron, JPMorgan Chase's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, referring to Hu's statements while in Washington.  \par \par \uc2 Traders had speculated that the bigger gains allowed in the yuan <CNY=CFXS> by the Chinese authorities earlier this month were aimed at pushing it through the 8-per-dollar mark before Hu's visit. But the yuan peaked at around 8.0022 per dollar on April 10. It was traded on Friday between 8.0140 and 8.0180.  \par \par \uc2 Traders had been expecting that Hu's meeting with U.S. President George W. Bush on Thursday would result in a commitment to a faster appreciation of the yuan. Hu said China would continue to liberalise the yuan regime but gave no specifics.  \par \par \uc2 That led to the yuan being sold in offshore forwards markets.  \par \par \uc2 But speculative positions in the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were small, Piron said, and hence any disappointment with Hu's comments was unlikely to result in a big sell-off.  \par \par \uc2 "If anything, the risk gets skewed to the other direction and we could see trade tensions and protectionist measures coming through. That is more of a slow-burning fuse and a Q3/Q4 risk to Asia and, potentially, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions," Piron said.  \par \par \uc2 Other analysts said the selling of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be limited ahead of the Group of Seven nations' meeting that starts on Friday and IMF meetings on the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 RUPIAH SUPPORTED  \par \par \uc2 Craig Chan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with the Royal Bank of Scotland, said equity flows into South Korean and Taiwan equity markets had been strong, underpinning those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but suspicion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  had capped the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Taiwan's stock market data showed foreigners have invested nearly a net $4.3 billion in the country's equity market so far in April.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> stopped short of hitting 1.6000 per U.S. dollar and stayed close to Wednesday's peak around 1.5960, which was its strongest in nearly 8 years.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah owed its strength to comments by Indonesia's chief economic minister Boediono on Thursday, that the authorities would let market forces guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that tight monetary policy would soon be relaxed, Chan said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> matched Thursday's high of 8,860 per dollar, its strongest since July 2004, before settling around 8,890/8,895. It is Asia's top performer this year, with gains of more than 10 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "Boediono opened the gates for more appreciation. That is stimulating more bond related inflows and pushing the equity market to record highs," Chan said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0800 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.60         117.59       -0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.5976         1.5972       -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      32.303         32.305       +0.01\par  Korean won      948.40         948.50       +0.01\par  Baht             37.85          37.74       -0.29\par  Peso             51.68          51.48       -0.39\par  Rupiah         8888.00        8880.00       -0.09\par  Rupee            45.11          45.11       +0.00\par  Ringgit         3.6583         3.6610       +0.07\par  Yuan            8.0170         8.0152       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.60         117.96       +0.31\par  Sing dlr        1.5976         1.6625       +4.06\par  Taiwan dlr      32.303         32.850       +1.69\par  Korean won      948.40        1011.60       +6.66\par  Baht             37.85          41.11       +8.61\par  Peso             51.68          53.09       +2.73\par  Rupiah         8888.00        9835.00      +10.65\par  Rupee            45.11          45.04       -0.16\par  Ringgit         3.6583         3.7790       +3.30\par  Yuan            8.0170         8.0702       +0.66\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060424e24l0005q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\p