\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Hits 8-Year High Before Suspected MAS Move  \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2006\par 09:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar hit a fresh eight-yearhigh in Asia Wednesday on hopes U.S. rate increases will soon end, before suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared some of the gains.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices rallied, tracking gains in U.S. Treasurys overnight following the release of the minutes of the Federal Open Market Committee's meeting that signaled an early end to U.S. monetary tightening, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0633 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.5983, off its near eight-year low of S$1.5975 in early trade, and compared with S$1.5989 at the close of New York trade. In late Asian trade Tuesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6021  \par \par \uc2 A Singapore dealer said stop-losses were triggered very early in the session after the U.S. dollar breached the S$1.5990 level.  \par \par \uc2 This pushed the greenback to a low of S$1.5975 - the lowest since May 6, 1998, when the pair had dipped to S$1.5827.  \par \par \uc2 At that juncture suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented further gains in the local dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 An MAS spokesperson told Dow Jones Newswires the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on its money-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The main reason for the rise Wednesday in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Singapore dollar was the belief that the end of the Fed's rate tightening phase will trigger another spell of weakness for the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Most members thought that the end of the tightening process was likely to be near, and some expressed concerns about the dangers of tightening too much, given the lags in the effects of policy," according to the FOMC minutes, released after a normal three-week period Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Reacting to such expectations, the greenback briefly hit a seven-month low of $1.2369 to the euro on the EBS dealing system, while it dropped to a two-week low of Y116.76 versus the Japanese yen in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 However, Philip Wee, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS Bank, said more gains in the Singapore dollar were likely capped since it had moved toward the stronger end of the MAS trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in the past defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it breaches the stronger or weaker end of the undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The rally in government bond prices was led by the 10-year paper, which led to a flattening of the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year bond yield fell five basis points to 3.58%, while the two-year yield dropped three basis points to 3.08%.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Latest  Previous \par Overnight Rate       2.876%   2.69% \par Two-year bond yield  3.08%    3.11% \par 10-year bond yield   3.53%    3.58% \par Two-year swap offer  3.60%    3.61% \par 10-year swap offer   3.97%    3.93% \par 2-10-yr swap spread: 37 bps   32 bps \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.