\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dlr Stronger Late; Bonds Up On SGD-Linked Flows  \b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2006\par 10:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar extended gains in Asia Thursday, as players stayed long on the local unit ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy review next week.  \par \par \uc2 But larger gains were capped after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight when the U.S. dollar fell to near an eight-year low.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices were stronger for a third straight day as foreign players targeted the shorter-end of the yield curve to take advantage of the strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0704 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6059, below S$1.6070 at the New York close Wednesday. The U.S. dollar was at S$1.6072 in late Asian trade Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a foreign bank said the local unit consolidated in a narrow range after Wednesday's volatile trade, when most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied.  \par \par \uc2 He said the next key support for the U.S. dollar was at S$1.600, while it should find resistance at S$1.6120.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar dropped to S$1.6016 overnight - the lowest since June 1998, when the greenback hit S$1.5890.  \par \par \uc2 JPMorgan said in a note that the Singapore dollar's testing of the stronger side of the MAS trading band is a signal for an impending move at next week's policy meeting.  \par \par \uc2 If the MAS tightens monetary policy in its half-yearly statement on April 11, it would be either allowing a one-time upward shift of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band or choosing a steeper appreciation, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current stance is to allow a modest and gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted exchange rate - a policy adopted in April 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The Asian Development Bank said in a report that it expects the MAS to maintain its 'moderately' tight monetary policy in view of strengthening domestic demand and increasing inflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered inflows into the shorter-end of the yield curve, lifting prices of two-year bonds and easing the overnight rate.  \par \par \uc2 The two-year yield dropped two basis points to 3.14%, while the 10-year yield slipped one basis point to 3.56%, steepening the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 'A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sparked (foreign) fund flows into the Singapore bond market,' said a dealer at a local bank.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps. \par                      Latest  Previous \par Overnight Rate       2.87%   3.09% \par Two-year bond yield  3.14%   3.16% \par 10-year bond yield   3.56%   3.57% \par Two-year swap offer  3.62%   3.60% \par 10-year swap offer   3.87%   3.85% \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2-10-yr swap spread: 25 BPS 25 BPS Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\uc2 \f2  -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Graham Norris -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060406e246006vk\par }\