\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firmer but wary of c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe  \par \uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 03:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , March 17 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against a generally soft dollar on Friday, but gains in the Malaysian ringgit and Indian rupee were curbed by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Wariness that \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step into the market to cap gains in the Singapore dollar <SGD=>, pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off a two-week high hit in early trade although traders said there had been no signs of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were underpinned as investors trimmed expectations for further U.S. dollar-friendly interest rate increases following tame U.S. inflation data on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2  A rise in the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> to its highest level since last July's revaluation and speculation over further gains also supported Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  In Kuala Lumpur, traders said that banks acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought dollars for ringgit <MYR=>. This capped the ringgit's gains at the psychologically important 3.70 per dollar level -- the strongest level since a peg against the dollar was abandoned last July.  \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not want to see the ringgit strengthen too far, too fast, although the trend for a stronger ringgit remained.  \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's Second Finance Minister Nor Mohamed Yakcop said on Friday that a higher ringgit would result in lower imported inflation.  \par \par \uc2  "This is the first ringgit comment from a senior official in a while, but given that it comes at a time when dollar/ringgit is trying to push to new year lows below 3.7000 it will be seen as a green light for further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength," said Shahab Jalinoos, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee <INR=IN> was pushed off a one-week high at 44.34 per dollar on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2  SING DOLLAR OFF HIGHS  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=> hit a two-week high at 1.6165 per U.S. dollar before trimming gains as investors suspected that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar was probably trading at the strong end of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. The MAS conducts monetary policy by guiding the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within an undisclosed trading band.  \par \par \uc2  It has a tightening stance of allowing "a modest and gradual appreciation" of the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tighten monetary policy further next month.  \par \par \uc2  "I am surprised that there hasn't been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the top half of the band," said Mirza Baig, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2  "This may be because the policy review is coming up and they don't want to do anything ahead of that."  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a two-week high at 970.4 per dollar. The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, which hit its highest level since January 2005 on Wednesday, inched lower. A Jakarta trader said the slight weakness was due to a covering of short positions on the dollar ahead of the weekend.  \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=> hovered around 39.06 per dollar, trading firmer with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained vulnerable to political uncertainty in Thailand.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0813 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.66         117.65       +0.85\par  Sing dlr        1.6183         1.6197       +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      32.426         32.445       +0.06\par  Korean won      970.80         975.00       +0.43\par  Baht             39.06          39.09       +0.08\par  Peso             50.97          51.14       +0.33\par  Rupiah         9163.00        9162.00       -0.01\par  Rupee            44.42          44.44       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.7045         3.7030       -0.04\par  Yuan            8.0316         8.0390       +0.09\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.66         117.96       +1.11\par  Sing dlr        1.6183         1.6625       +2.73\par  Taiwan dlr      32.426         32.850       +1.31\par  Korean won      970.80        1011.60  