\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Up On Yen; Bonds Down On Treasurys  \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 07:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar strengthened Tuesday, reacting to a stronger Japanese yen, but further gains were capped due to fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows if DBS Bank succeeds in its effort to buy South Korea's fifth-biggest lender.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices declined after prices of U.S. Treasurys dropped overnight on continued fears of higher U.S. interest rates, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0611 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6250, compared with S$1.6254 at the close of New York trade Monday. The U.S. dollar was at S$1.6278 in Asian trade late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback traded between S$1.6236 and S$1.6262.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a foreign bank said interbank players stepped in after the U.S. dollar dipped to S$1.6240 in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 News that DBS will bid for a 50.5% stake in Korea Exchange Bank, which is controlled by U.S. Lone Star Funds, also lent support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair after some estimated that the bid could be around US$6 billion, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts don't expect DBS to emerge the winner, as it faces tough competition from two South Korean lenders.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts were also wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is trading 1.3% above its midpoint on a trade-weighted basis.  \par \par \uc2 One reason for its surge is the recent decoupling from movements in the Japanese yen, which has been volatile since the Bank of Japan's recent tightening of monetary policy, JPMorgan said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.25%      3.063% \par Two-year bond yield   3.14%      3.12% \par 10-year bond yield    3.55%      3.54% \par Two-year swap offer   3.65%      3.62% \par 10-year swap offer    3.86%      3.84% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  21 BPs     22 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 14-03-06 0650GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060314e23e00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
