\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat Late Despite Weaker Yen, Bonds Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 08:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was little changed Monday despite a weaker yen as there was little corporate demand for the U.S. dollar after recent flows from mergers and acquisitions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds fell across the board. The slide was led by the front end, which helped to flatten the yield curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0618 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6278, compared with S$1.6279 at the close of New York trade Friday. The U.S. dollar was at S$1.6297 in Asian trade late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback traded between S$1.6258 and S$1.6294.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a foreign bank said that corporates stepped back after they realized there was little demand out there for the U.S. dollar on speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions needed for Temasek's proposed purchase of Thailand's Shin Corp had already been put through.  \par \par \uc2 He said that some corporates also sold the greenback early in the session before it stabilized to current flat levels.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they expect some more corporate inflows over the next few days from mergers and acquisitions taking place in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 One such inflow could come from theproposed sale of SembCorp Industries' 60% stake in SembCorp Logistics to Australia's Toll Holdings for S$749 million. If SembCorp accepts Toll's full takeover offer, the transaction could be worth S$1.4 billion.  \par \par \uc2 However, JPMorgan cautioned in a note Monday that recent gains in the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted exchange rate are unlikely to continue because of fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite broad expectations that it might move to a tighter policy in April.  \par \par \uc2 It said the Singapore dollar is 1.20% above the midpoint of the band, but it faces strong support if it slips to 0.7% above midpoint.  \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, the two-year yield rose six basis points to 3.11%, reacting to stronger-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls data, which raised expectations the Federal Reserve may push benchmark rates above 5% from 4.5% now.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year yield rose two basis points to 3.52%, which helped flatten the yield curve by another four basis points to 41 points.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.063%     3.063% \par Two-year bond yield   3.11%      3.05% \par 10-year bond yield    3.52%      3.50% \par Two-year swap offer   3.62%      3.59% \par 10-year swap offer    3.84%      3.83% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  22 BPs     24 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 13-03-06 0731GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060313e23d0009l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
