\par\par \b \uc2 Sing dollar hits highest more than 7 yrs vs USD  \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 01:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 3 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit its highest levels in more than 7 years in overnight deals as foreign investors poured money into Asian assets, leading to sharp gains in one of the region's more liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said a breach of resistance around 1.6160-1.6170 per U.S. dollar on Thursday triggered some stop-loss buying of Sing dollars.  \par \par \uc2 It was traded as high as 1.6127 per U.S. dollar, a level last seen in October 1998 towards the end of the Asian financial crisis, and has risen 1.5 percent in two weeks. On Friday morning it was trading around 1.6140.  \par \par \uc2 "We saw stops go out yesterday after the highs of the previous two runs were taken out," Callum Henderson, Standard Chartered Bank's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, said.  \par \par \uc2 Henderson said rises in the Thai baht <THB=>, Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, South Korean won <KRW=> showed foreigners were keen on Asian assets. Yet they were being selective, and the Singapore dollar was perceived to be a low-risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders have been wary of buying the Sing dollar for fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given market estimates that it is trading near the top of its secret trade-weighted policy band.  \par \par \uc2 Henderson said the top end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band as per his estimates was now around 1.61 per U.S. dollar. That estimates assumes the band is 3 percent wide and its mid-point appreciates at an annual pace of 2 percent.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060303e23300024\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
