\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears;Bonds Lower  \b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 09:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2006, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was slightly weaker in Asia Thursday on fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent more gains and on a slight recovery in the U.S. dollar against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds fell across the board after overnight weakness in U.S. Treasurys and on local corporate issuance in the primary market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0647 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6187, up from S$1.6178 in New York trade Wednesday. It was at S$1.6203 in Asian trade Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a Singapore bank said foreign funds sold the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar early in the session, but the selling halted after talk emerged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A second dealer said talk that the MAS was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.6170-S$1.6180 forced speculators to step back.  \par \par \uc2 The early push for a stronger Singapore dollar was due to renewed speculation that China and Malaysia may allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The speculation rose as U.S. Undersecretary of Treasury for International Affairs Timothy Adams reiterated Wednesday the U.S. view that China needs to introduce more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.  \par \par \uc2 Jimmy Koh, treasury economist at United Overseas Bank, said that in the medium term the Singapore dollar will continue to face upward pressure because of hopes China may allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise.  \par \par \uc2 He said unwinding of carry trades was also helping the Japanese yen and as a result pushing up Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Speculation about further monetary tightening by the MAS in its next policy review due in April is another factor pushing the Singapore dollar higher, Koh said.  \par \par \uc2 'We think they will not jump the gun. Inflation is not running away therefore there's no need to further tighten policy,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 The next key level for the U.S. dollar is S$1.6162 - the lowest level for the greenback last year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 'This is a critical level that the market will be watching closely,' said Koh.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In the bond market, weaker U.S. Treasurys and the issue of new corporate debt weighed on the market. \par   Southeast Asia's biggest property company, CapitaLand Ltd., sold S$200 million in fixed- and floating-rate five-year bonds Thursday. \par   Earlier in the day, Frasers Centrepoint sold S$200 million five-year bonds at 4.045%, a source familiar with the deal said. \par   The bond sales had the biggest impact on the five-year government bond, whose yield rose five basis points to 2.33%, while the two-year yield climbed six basis points to 2.91%. \par   The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps: \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.125%   3.1875% \par Two-year bond yield   2.91%     2.85% \par 10-year bond yield    3.52%     3.49% \par Two-year swap offer   3.60%     3.55% \par 10-year swap offer    3.78%     3.73% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  18 BPs    18 BPs \par   Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Mary de Wet -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020060302e232005v6\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs